  "hints": [
    "Keep the pending calls as data (floor and kind) in request order, and let the controller own the floor, the sweep direction and the status. A policy should only answer two questions about that data.",
    "Give each policy serve(car) (should the doors open here, and which calls does that satisfy?) and heading(car) (which way to move, or none). tick() is then the same for both: serve, else heading and move one floor, then serve again.",
    "For LOOK, a stop is wanted if it is a car call or a hall call in the sweep direction; when nothing lies ahead, a hall call in the other direction is served too and the sweep reverses. FCFS only ever looks at stops[0]. Look the policy up in a table by name."
  ],
  "complexity": {
    "time": "O(P) per tick for P pending calls",
    "space": "O(P)"
  }
}
